{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Snippet: Project Card
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ONE card implementation, two sources. `otodor-projects` can read its
  entries from a Shopify blog (an article per project) or from section
  blocks, and both hand their fields to this snippet — so a change to how a
  project looks is made once, and the two sources can never drift apart.
  That is the same arrangement `otodor-category-card` has with the three
  sources of the category selector.

  Parameters (all optional except title):
    title      — project name.                                  [required]
    meta       — the line under it: location, door type, year.
    text       — one supporting sentence. Clamped to 3 lines.
    image      — cover image. Also the poster frame for a video.
    video      — a Shopify-hosted video (Content → Files).       [wins]
    video_url  — a direct .mp4 / .webm / .mov URL.               [2nd]
    link       — makes the whole card a link. Blank = static card.
    sizes      — the `sizes` attribute for the cover image.

  MEDIA CASCADE: video → video_url → image. A card with none of the three
  still renders — a project with a name and a location is worth listing —
  but the media frame collapses rather than leaving an empty grey box.

  NOTHING AUTOPLAYS. A projects gallery is browsed, not scrolled past, and
  a wall of self-playing installation films is a bandwidth bill and a
  motion-sickness complaint. Videos carry real controls and `preload="none"`,
  so a visitor who never presses play never downloads a frame.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign has_media = false
  if video != blank or video_url != blank or image != blank
    assign has_media = true
  endif
  assign is_video = false
  if video != blank or video_url != blank
    assign is_video = true
  endif
  assign card_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 990px) 33vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 80vw'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  A linked card is a stretched overlay link — EXCEPT when it holds a video,
  where an overlay would sit on top of the player's own controls. There the
  title becomes the link instead. Not a zero-size overlay: that leaves a
  focusable element with no visible target, which is worse than no link.
{%- endcomment -%}
<article class="otodor-project{% if is_video %} otodor-project--video{% endif %}">
  {%- if link != blank and is_video == false -%}
    <a class="otodor-project__link" href="{{ link }}" aria-label="{{ title | escape }}"></a>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if has_media -%}
    <div class="otodor-project__frame">
      {%- if video != blank -%}
        {{
          video
          | video_tag:
            image_size: '1400x',
            autoplay: false,
            loop: false,
            muted: true,
            controls: true,
            playsinline: true,
            preload: 'none',
            class: 'otodor-project__media'
        }}
      {%- elsif video_url != blank -%}
        <video
          class="otodor-project__media"
          controls muted playsinline preload="none"
          {% if image != blank %}poster="{{ image | image_url: width: 1400 }}"{% endif %}
        >
          <source src="{{ video_url }}">
        </video>
      {%- else -%}
        {{
          image
          | image_url: width: 1400
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'lazy',
            widths: '400, 700, 1000, 1400',
            sizes: card_sizes,
            class: 'otodor-project__media',
            alt: title
        }}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A video card says so before it is clicked, and says it in text as
        well as in shape — the badge is not a play triangle alone.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if is_video -%}
        <span class="otodor-project__badge">Video</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="otodor-project__body">
    {%- if meta != blank -%}
      <span class="otodor-project__meta">{{ meta | escape }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <h3 class="otodor-project__title">
      {%- if link != blank and is_video -%}
        <a class="otodor-project__title-link" href="{{ link }}">{{ title | escape }}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        {{ title | escape }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </h3>
    {%- if text != blank -%}
      <p class="otodor-project__text">{{ text | strip_html | truncate: 160 }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</article>
